From bc57fc4fdab5768c828befe88085ef5cc46215b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 18:37:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fydroid: Mojo C2 hooks - c2.mojo* names + pluggable
 decoder factory

Minimal upstream hooks (hybrid policy) so fydroid's Mojo C2 path can reuse the
decode component while the Mojo backends/store live in libfydroid_c2_mojo:

- common/V4L2ComponentCommon.cpp: rename component name VALUES from c2.v4l2.*
  to c2.mojo.* (encoders) / c2.mojo-legacy.* (decoders) to match fydroid's
  media_codecs_c2.xml. All name->codec mapping compares the k* symbols, never
  literals, so this one file re-labels the whole reused decode path. VP8/VP9
  encoder symbols kept (renamed) so the unused upstream V4L2 store/encode path
  still compiles.
- V4L2DecodeComponent: add a pluggable DecoderFactoryCB (SetDecoderFactory),
  defaulting to V4L2Decoder::Create. libfydroid_c2_mojo overrides it with
  MojoDecoder::Create so the reused component talks Mojo IPC instead of
  /dev/video*, with zero Mojo/arc deps leaking into libv4l2_codec2_components.

Local commit only (not pushed); regenerated into device/fydeos patch files
later. See device/fydeos/docs/c2-codec2-mojo-port-plan.md.

Change-Id: Idabf4b545018a78b060eec0dd039d75f46135f5f
